{%- comment -%}
  A layout group — the one block that arranges other blocks.

  **This is the primitive the theme was missing.** Merchant blocks render as one
  flat sibling flow, so until now anything the design puts *side by side* could
  not be built from blocks at all: the products list's eyebrow and its "View
  All" share one `space-between` row, and as plain blocks they fell onto two
  lines. Every workaround for that was a section-specific rule in the
  stylesheet. A group replaces all of them with something a merchant can see and
  move.

  It belongs to no section. Any section that renders `{% content_for 'blocks' %}`
  can list `group`, and the group takes `@theme` — every theme block there is —
  so what goes inside it is the merchant's business, not the section's.

  **Horizontal is the default, deliberately.** A vertical group adds nothing
  over simply placing the blocks one after another, which is what a flat flow
  already gives; the reason to reach for a group is to put things on one row.
  Vertical earns its place only *nested inside a horizontal group* — a column
  of two things sitting on a row — because inside a row that free stacking is
  gone.

  **Three settings are horizontal-only and say so with `visible_if`**, rather
  than sitting in the panel doing nothing:

    - `gap` resolves to `column-gap`, which a column never uses — a stacked
      group takes its spacing from the section, by design.
    - `wrap` is meaningless in a column: wrapping one needs a bounded height,
      and nothing here gives it one.
    - `stack_below` exists to turn a row into a column, so it has nothing to
      say to a group that already is one.

  `distribute` and `align` stay visible throughout: both axes are real in
  either direction, and only which one they act on changes.

  The children's own vertical margins are zeroed, the same way
  `.collection-list__content` zeroes them: a gap and a margin add, so a block
  carrying both would space itself twice. They keep those margins everywhere
  else, which is why this is done here rather than at the source.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign direction = 'row'
  if block.settings.direction == 'vertical'
    assign direction = 'column'
  endif

  comment
    **`distribute` is a row's setting only, and that is a fact about height.**
    It sets `justify-content`, the *main* axis — vertical in a column — and the
    group is only ever as tall as its contents, so there is no free space there
    to distribute and every value behaves identically. It is hidden in a column
    and pinned to the start rather than left to a stored value that does
    nothing.

    Strictly it can act on a column that has been *stretched* taller than its
    contents, which needs the group nested in a row aligning `stretch`. That is
    rare, invisible when it is not happening, and not worth a control that does
    nothing the rest of the time.
  endcomment
  assign justify = 'flex-start'
  unless block.settings.direction == 'vertical'
    case block.settings.distribute
      when 'center'
        assign justify = 'center'
      when 'end'
        assign justify = 'flex-end'
      when 'between'
        assign justify = 'space-between'
    endcase
  endunless

  comment
    Two align settings, one per direction, because a select cannot hide an
    individual option and `baseline` is not one a column can honour — in a
    column the cross axis is horizontal, and baseline alignment there falls back
    to start. Offering it was offering a choice that silently did nothing.
  endcomment
  assign align_choice = block.settings.align
  if block.settings.direction == 'vertical'
    assign align_choice = block.settings.align_vertical
  endif

  case align_choice
    when 'center'
      assign align = 'center'
    when 'end'
      assign align = 'flex-end'
    when 'stretch'
      assign align = 'stretch'
    when 'start'
      assign align = 'flex-start'
    else
      assign align = 'baseline'
  endcase

  assign wrap = 'wrap'
  unless block.settings.wrap
    assign wrap = 'nowrap'
  endunless

  comment
    **The gap is emitted as `--group-gap`, deliberately not as `--block-gap`.**

    `block-spacing` writes `--block-gap`, and the section wrapper above writes
    the same property to state its own vertical rhythm. Custom properties
    inherit, so a group writing `--block-gap` *shadows the section's* for
    everything inside it — which is how a stacked group ended up spacing its
    children by its own horizontal setting instead of the section's rhythm, and
    sat visibly out of step with the gap above it.

    Under its own name the section's value survives inheritance, and the
    stylesheet can spend each on the axis it belongs to: this on `column-gap`,
    the section's on `row-gap`. So the setting is horizontal only, and a group
    that stacks — by choice or because the container query fired — falls back
    into the section's rhythm with nothing to configure.

    The step guard is `block-spacing`'s own: an unrecognised value prints
    nothing rather than `var(--step-)`, which would be invalid and take the
    whole declaration with it. `none` prints `0`.
  endcomment
  assign gap_steps = 'minimal,tiny,small,medium,large,xlarge' | split: ','
  assign gap_css = ''
  if block.settings.gap == 'none'
    assign gap_css = '--group-gap: 0;'
  elsif gap_steps contains block.settings.gap
    assign gap_css = '--group-gap: var(--step-' | append: block.settings.gap | append: ');'
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  **Two elements, and that is not a wrapper for its own sake.** The group has
  to answer a question about its own width — "am I narrow enough to stack?" —
  and a container cannot be styled by a query against itself. So the outer
  element *is* the container and the inner one is the row that responds. This
  theme has hit that trap twice already, on `.row-carousel__frame` and on
  `.quick-view__frame`: put both on one element and it parses, uploads and
  silently never fires.

  A container query rather than a media query, deliberately. The group should
  stack when *it* is narrow — in a half-width column on a desktop just as much
  as on a phone — which is a question about the block, not the screen.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="layout-group"
  data-stack="{{ block.settings.stack_below }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div
    class="layout-group__inner"
    style="--group-direction: {{ direction }}; --group-justify: {{ justify }}; --group-align: {{ align }}; --group-wrap: {{ wrap }};{{ gap_css }}"
  >
    {% content_for 'blocks' %}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.group.name",
  "tag": null,
  "blocks": [{ "type": "@theme" }, { "type": "@app" }],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "direction",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.direction.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.direction.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "horizontal", "label": "t:blocks.group.direction.horizontal" },
        { "value": "vertical", "label": "t:blocks.group.direction.vertical" }
      ],
      "default": "horizontal"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "distribute",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.distribute.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.distribute.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:blocks.group.distribute.start" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:blocks.group.distribute.center" },
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:blocks.group.distribute.end" },
        { "value": "between", "label": "t:blocks.group.distribute.between" }
      ],
      "default": "between",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.direction == 'horizontal' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "align",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.align.label_horizontal",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.align.info_horizontal",
      "options": [
        { "value": "baseline", "label": "t:blocks.group.align.text" },
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:blocks.group.align.top" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:blocks.group.align.middle" },
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:blocks.group.align.bottom" },
        { "value": "stretch", "label": "t:blocks.group.align.equal_height" }
      ],
      "default": "baseline",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.direction == 'horizontal' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "align_vertical",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.align.label_vertical",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.align.info_vertical",
      "options": [
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:blocks.group.align.left" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:blocks.group.align.centre" },
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:blocks.group.align.right" },
        { "value": "stretch", "label": "t:blocks.group.align.full_width" }
      ],
      "default": "start",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.direction == 'vertical' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "wrap",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.wrap.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.wrap.info",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.direction == 'horizontal' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "stack_below",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.stack_below.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.stack_below.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "never", "label": "t:blocks.group.stack_below.never" },
        { "value": "tablet", "label": "t:blocks.group.stack_below.tablet" },
        { "value": "mobile", "label": "t:blocks.group.stack_below.mobile" }
      ],
      "default": "mobile",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.direction == 'horizontal' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.all.spacing_header",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.direction == 'horizontal' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.gap.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.gap.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.direction == 'horizontal' }}",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.none" },
        { "value": "minimal", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.minimal" },
        { "value": "tiny", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.tiny" },
        { "value": "small", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.small" },
        { "value": "medium", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.medium" },
        { "value": "large", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.large" },
        { "value": "xlarge", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.xlarge" }
      ],
      "default": "medium"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.group.name",
      "settings": {
        "direction": "horizontal",
        "distribute": "between",
        "align": "baseline",
        "wrap": true,
        "stack_below": "mobile",
        "gap": "medium"
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
